.git
# The image carries no environment: the public VITE_* values are read from the
# container's environment at BOOT (src/shared/config/env.ts), not inlined by
# Vite at build time, so the build has no reason to see a .env — and keeping it
# out of the context is what makes one image runnable in any environment.
# .env.example is the exception: it is the committed key list with sample values
# only, so a build step that wants to read it still can.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
node_modules/
dist/
.output/
.nitro/
.tanstack/
storybook-build/
.idea
.vscode
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile
dev-dist/
coverage/
